News Flow — The Common-Sense License
=====================================

Version 1.0, September 2026

This project was written by an AI (Buffy, via Codebuff) at the direction of a
human operator, and it carries the simplest license its author could legally
draft. Not MIT, not GPL — something custom, because the whole codebase is
custom too. Call it the **Common-Sense License**.

Definitions
-----------

  "The Software"  — News Flow: every file in this repository, including the
                    source code, templates, fixtures, scripts, and this
                    license itself.
  "You"           — anyone who has obtained a copy of The Software.
  "The Authors"   — the AI that wrote it and the human who told it to,
                    jointly. Blame is shared; so is credit.

Grant
-----

Permission is granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of The
Software to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell,
and/or ship copies of The Software, in source or compiled form, for any
purpose whatsoever — commercial, personal, educational, or a hobby project
you abandon in three weeks — subject to the following conditions:

  1. Include this license (or a link to it) with any substantial portion of
     The Software you distribute.

  2. Change it, break it, fork it, rename it — just don't pretend you wrote
     the original. Keep the notice "Based on News Flow" somewhere reasonable
     in your derivative.

  3. If you fix a bug, that fix is yours. If you introduce one, that bug is
     also yours. The Authors accept credit only for the original state.

The Fine Print
--------------

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED — INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. In plain terms: it
scrapes news sites; news sites change their markup at 2 a.m.; things will
break. That is not a warranty breach; that is web scraping.

IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER
LIABILITY — including lost data, missed deadlines, angry editors, duplicate
WordPress posts, or the existential realization that your news aggregator
curation pipeline now has a license written by the same AI that wrote its
database migrations — whether arising from contract, tort, or otherwise,
in connection with The Software or its use.

Additional terms
----------------

- Scraping: The Software fetches publicly available web pages. What you do
  with the fetched content is your responsibility, not the Authors'.
- Attribution of scraped content belongs to the original publishers. Be kind
  to them; they wrote the articles your pipeline exists to process.
- If The Software brings you joy, consider fixing someone else's bug today.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED WITH LOVE, PROMPTS, AND TOKENS.
